      "solution": "1. Select **Virtual machines** in the portal menu, then **+ Create**.\n2. **Basics**: Resource group **Create new** → `rg-web-dev`; Virtual machine name `vm-web-01`; Region **(Europe) West Europe**; Image **Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS - x64 Gen2**; Size **Standard_B2s**; Authentication **SSH public key**; Public inbound ports **Allow selected ports** → **SSH (22)** and **HTTP (80)**.\n3. **Disks**: OS disk type **Standard SSD (LRS)**.\n4. **Networking**: keep **(new) pip-web-dev** and the **Basic** NIC network security group.\n5. **Management**: turn on **Enable auto-shutdown**, time `19:00`.\n6. **Tags**: env = `dev`, owner = `training`.\n7. **Review + create** → **Create**, then **Go to resource**.\n8. Select **Stop** (or run `az vm deallocate -g rg-web-dev -n vm-web-01` in Cloud Shell) so the status becomes **Stopped (deallocated)**."
